  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Rain chances remain limited through midweek, \naccompanied by near to below normal temperatures. The next best \nchance for precipitation arrives Wednesday night into Thursday.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nShortwave energy should cross the region on Tuesday bringing \ncloud cover, and a slight chance of isolated showers, that will \nreduce high temps and increase low temps. Dry conditions with \nbelow normal low temps will continue to Wednesday night. \n\nEnsemble models show increasing consistency in gusty winds from\nthe LLJ on Wednesday night. In addition, ensembles show \nincreasing confidence in a large closed low pressure system \nmoving across Canada that could bring some soaking rain. \nHowever, significant uncertainty on the track and timing of the \nlow exists across all deterministic models.",
